  "description": "T6 - Silver birch - Fell to ground level and replace with 12-14g Magnolia. Reason for work: The existing Silver Birch is proposed for removal in accordance with recommendations contained within a recent arboricultural report, which identified the tree as unsuitable for long-term retention in its current location. The tree has been previously subject to poor pruning practices, including topping, which has resulted in weak structural form, irregular regrowth, and an increased likelihood of future management issues. Although the tree is not currently in physiological decline, its structural integrity and quality have been adversely affected by historic poor management. Due to its form, growth habit, and position within the site, the tree is no longer considered appropriate to retain as a long-term specimen. Continued retention would require ongoing intervention and would not be sustainable from an arboricultural or management perspective. It is proposed to replace the tree with a 12???14cm girth Magnolia, which is more suitable for the scale and setting of the site. The replacement will provide long-term amenity value while offering a form and growth habit more compatible with the surrounding environment. This replacement planting will ensure no net loss of amenity and will represents a sustainable improvement to the site???s arboricultural quality.",
